  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_010: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. All completed multiprofile experiments use scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder; scgpt has never been tested in any completed experiment. In singleprofile, scvi_n200 outperformed pca_n2000, but scgpt remains uncharacterized. Question: config_038 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) identical to the current best. This isolates the effect of RNA representation in the top-performing regime. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against the incumbent leader, directly testing whether an alternative learned RNA encoder (scgpt) can improve upon scvi_n200 in the setting that already shows the strongest performance. If scgpt matches or exceeds config_010, it opens a new exploitation direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and redirects budget toward other levers (e.g., aggregation or fusion refinements). No other available configuration provides as direct a test of the single largest unexplored variable in the current best configuration."
}

